WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.860
Respect! Welcome back to Serious Topics, where today, with all due respect, I am competing with RTS.

2
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.660
Before us is a very complicated and controversial event, the Second World War, specifically how and why it started.

3
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:24.200
Unlike the Great War, where we have an undisputed and clear sequence of events that led to the Austro-Hungarian attack on Serbia, historians do not agree about the exact course of events that led to the start of the greatest human catastrophe ever.

4
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:50.930
The First World War ended, and four empires fell: the German, Austro-Hungarian, Russian and Ottoman.

5
00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:53.390
And it was time for the winners to take their spoils.

6
00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:59.520
A series of peace negotiations followed in which the Allies imposed hard-to-meet demands on the losers.

7
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.890
I served that to you nicely in a video too, link at the top right.

8
00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:09.450
Because of the imposed demands, those who found themselves on the wrong side of history had to hand over a lot of land.

9
00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.820
They also had to pay a huge pile of money for war reparations.

10
00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.820
Germany was obliged to pay what today is the equivalent of 250 billion dollars.

11
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.230
Now you say: well, that is Germany, what is that to them?

12
00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:22.530
Well, it was not like that.

13
00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:25.110
Germany simply did not have that money.

14
00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.830
And what do you do when you do not have enough money?

15
00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:29.770
You can print more money.

16
00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:41.600
Thanks to this intriguing move, the value of German money became equal to toilet paper, which is a joke that does not apply during a pandemic, but you get what I mean.

17
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.100
One American dollar was worth 4200 billion German marks.

18
00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.670
And as the money lost its value, the German economy fell apart.

19
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:57.380
Their bank was going under, unemployment rose dizzyingly and among the people hostility began to spread sharply toward the countries that imposed that debt.

20
00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.630
Wait, a baby. Come in, come in, how cute.

21
00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.090
You will regret saying that in a couple of seconds.

22
00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:06.560
This baby will take part in the First World War on Germany's side in a couple of decades.

23
00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:15.470
As the Central Powers collapsed, the failed painter developed a special hatred toward the winners, but at the same time toward two ethnic groups, Jews and Slavs.

24
00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:17.670
This was not that strange for the 20th century.

25
00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.830
Nationalism from the previous century grew into fascism in some countries.

26
00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:26.220
I know many do not get that these are two very different concepts, but more on that later.

27
00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:47.480
Adolf Hitler blamed the Jews for the German economic situation, and since he was a skilled demagogue, and do not take that as a compliment, by the 1930 elections he had managed to secure 6 million voters, while by November 33 he would collect as many as 92% of the votes, because there was not a single other party anyway.

28
00:02:47.680 --> 00:03:04.430
Earlier that year the president of Germany, Paul von Hindenburg, uh, I pronounced him well, man, kudos, Hindenburg, because of Hitler's sudden rise in popularity, had to appoint him chancellor, after which the latter immediately banned the multiparty system, which made it easier to carry out his radical measures.

29
00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:09.220
Burning of books, shooting of political opponents and, of course, persecution of Jews.

30
00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.390
Now nothing could stop Hitler's rise anymore.

31
00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:18.150
Of course, I am skipping a lot of things because I have to squeeze all this into 20 minutes, but you get it, it was very bad.

32
00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:23.910
In 1934 Hindenburg dies, which Hitler uses to seize complete power in the state and establish a dictatorship.

33
00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:28.060
This period was marked by a dizzying rise of fascist sentiment in society.

34
00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:37.900
The German people were systematically taught that they belonged to a superior Aryan race, in which they also ranked other Nordic peoples, while all the rest were considered a lesser race.

35
00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:45.280
The Second World War was the worst event in the history of humanity and all of it happened only 80 years ago, so keep that in mind.

36
00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:51.740
But there you go, Europe was gripped by fanatical regimes and it was only a matter of time before it would erupt again.

37
00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.340
In any case, let us not rush.

38
00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.650
Somewhere else in Europe there are people with similar thinking.

39
00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:01.070
Now we go a bit further south to visit a man who wanted to bring back the Roman Empire.

40
00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:05.440
Only, unfortunately, not in the game Age of Civilizations, but it was Benito Mussolini.

41
00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.350
Fascism was trending in Italy since the beginning of the 20s.

42
00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:09.680
Why?

43
00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.130
Italy had been promised a lot in the London Agreement of 1915.

44
00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:18.410
Yes, the one in which the French and British wanted to create a big Serbia, that one, comments above, I know.

45
00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:23.130
Well, in that agreement they promised the Italians many parts of the Adriatic coast in the Balkans.

46
00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:29.860
However, Italy did not really prove itself in the war, so those territories were ceded to some other kingdom, Yugoslavia.

47
00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:38.890
True, those territories really had a good percentage of Italian population, which you can still see today in the architecture of the Croatian resorts.

48
00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:49.650
Tensions between Italy and Yugo rise, but also besides that, general dissatisfaction in the country because of the very bad economic situation was ideal for popularizing extreme ideologies.

49
00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:59.020
Taking that opportunity, Benito Mussolini carries out a coup and seizes power in 1922, and by 1925 de facto establishes a one-party totalitarian regime, in other words a dictatorship.

50
00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:03.800
Mussolini had far bigger goals, the conquest of Yugoslavia and the rest of the Balkans.

51
00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:04.510
Far bigger.

52
00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.040
Roman Empire level bigger.

53
00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.640
I mean, look at the guy's face, everything is clear to you.

54
00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:16.790
At first, Italy was not so hardline on the question of racism, but over time, hanging out with Germany had a bad influence on Benito.

55
00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:17.860
Choose your friends.

56
00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:29.130
As we said, using the catastrophic economic situation after the great war, Mussolini climbed to the top relatively quickly, but actually failed to fulfill his promises of GDP growth.

57
00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:35.980
In fact, the economy grows even more slowly, and from 1929 to 1933 the whole world was struck by the greatest economic crisis up to then.

58
00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:51.160
Although that no longer mattered, with his exceptional skill at spreading propaganda he intoxicated people with a story of a great Italian empire that would bring them all the wealth of the world, an empire in which the whole Mediterranean Sea would be Italian, mare nostrum, our sea.

59
00:05:51.520 --> 00:06:02.240
On the other hand, Hitler, who was a big Mussolini fan, I am not kidding, Hitler asked for Mussolini's picture with an autograph, everyone has their heroes, although it is rightly said that you should never meet your hero.

60
00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:13.140
Hitler raised the army to an enviable level, which the strongest powers of the time, France and Britain, noticed, but they were in the mood of: what is the worst that can happen?

61
00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.190
However, that was not the end of the reforms.

62
00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:22.180
Soon the arming of the country begins, and in the mid-30s he introduces mandatory military service.

63
00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:29.740
The reason why it was especially controversial is that the Treaty of Versailles forbade them to have more than 100,000 soldiers.

64
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.710
Luckily they were nowhere near that number.

65
00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:36.070
Nowhere near in the sense that they had over 4 million by 1939.

66
00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:38.270
The British and French do nothing.

67
00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:43.300
Almost the whole German economy was oriented toward the militarization of society.

68
00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:46.080
Unemployment fell from 30% to almost zero.

69
00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:54.000
Thanks to massive projects, such as building the famous autobahn system, as well as establishing world-famous conglomerates.

70
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.010
Okay, so, there is money, there is an army, there is hatred, aka a motive.

71
00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:00.120
It was time to start taking action.

72
00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:05.120
Well yes, the area around the river Rhine had to be returned under total German control.

73
00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:14.560
Under the Treaty of Versailles this extremely rich region, populated mainly by Germans, was temporarily under occupation by the Allies as a sort of reparation after the great war.

74
00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:20.330
Well, in 1936 Hitler sends 3000 soldiers and establishes undisputed power in the region.

75
00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:24.660
In response to this, the British and French do absolutely nothing.

76
00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:25.640
They did not want war.

77
00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:27.890
Because of that the balance of power in Europe shifts.

78
00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:31.660
These two slowly lose prestige, while the Third Reich gains strength at a terrifying speed.

79
00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.740
Okay, the Rhine is now undoubtedly Germany.

80
00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.260
I suppose that is that.

81
00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.060
Why would you make this video then?

82
00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.770
Now we encounter the key concept of Nazi ideology.

83
00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.410
Lebensraum, living space.

84
00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:49.200
The goal of the Nazi party was expansion to the east, onto the territories of present-day Poland, Ukraine and of course Russia.

85
00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:58.990
This territory would serve to feed the German people at the cost of the lives of its native Slavic population, which would be deported, starved or simply killed.

86
00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:02.250
So all of this would serve to feed just one people.

87
00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.020
All this happens only 80 years ago, do you understand?

88
00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:12.960
However, besides that crazy plan, there were still plenty of territories populated by Germans that were currently outside the Reich, such as Austria.

89
00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:21.340
German intellectuals had dreamed of uniting these two states for decades, but under the Treaty of Versailles that was not even allowed to cross their minds.

90
00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:31.020
However, as Hitler had already proven a couple of times that the British and French have no guts to do anything, nothing prevented him from simply annexing Austria in March 1938.

91
00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:39.770
Only after the annexation did he ask the people in Austria whether they actually wanted to unite with Germany, because he is above all a democrat.

92
00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:46.220
Of course, 99.73% of people said yes, and the Third Reich grew by about 90,000 km2 and 6,500,000 inhabitants.

93
00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:49.800
And what did the English and French do about that? Nothing.

94
00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.610
And then, why stop there when you are already on a roll?

95
00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:57.720
Namely, in the Sudeten region of the then Czechoslovakia lived another 3 million Germans.

96
00:08:57.880 --> 00:08:59.810
And where there is a German, there is Germany.

97
00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:04.570
Hitler used that excuse to justify the occupation of the Sudetenland in late 1938.

98
00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:10.600
And to everyone's wonder, aware that this leads to catastrophe, the British and French decided to do something.

99
00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:11.080
But what?

100
00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:18.940
Well, they convened a conference in Munich, where together with the Italians and Germans they reached an agreement about the Czechoslovak region.

101
00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:23.600
Only, somehow they forgot to invite Czechoslovakia itself to that conference.

102
00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.870
Oh well, my God, damn it, it happens, whatever.

103
00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:31.260
At the conference four states reached a compromise, which in fact was not a compromise.

104
00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:37.810
Hitler was allowed to take the Sudeten region without problems, and in return he put his hand on his heart and promised he would not expand any more.

105
00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:46.130
With this move, the British prime minister Neville Chamberlain considered that Hitler was satisfied, after which in London he proudly delivered his peace in our time speech.

106
00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:50.700
And everyone celebrated and lived happily ever after, Hitler nevertheless occupied the whole of Czechoslovakia.

107
00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:53.900
He made a protectorate out of Czechia, a puppet out of Slovakia.

108
00:09:53.900 --> 00:10:01.370
Seeing that nobody stops him from expanding, he sends an ultimatum to Lithuania to hand over to him a territory called, I am not kidding, Memelland.

109
00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.820
Okay, maybe it is pronounced Memelland, but do not take this away from me.

110
00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:08.000
Of course, they soon occupied Memelland from her, because who would not.

111
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.180
Meanwhile, Mussolini also gobbled up territories.

112
00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:14.980
Enormous Ethiopia, then Eritrea, Somalia, from 1935 to 1937.

113
00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:19.660
Now, why these territories, when they do not reach the Mediterranean as he first wanted?

114
00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:26.200
Maybe to regain his prestige after failed economic reforms, and maybe simply because he can.

115
00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:30.910
The British, French and others said that it was not nice, but guess what they did.

116
00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:31.270
Nothing.

117
00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:41.100
Mussolini certainly did not like being nagged for these conquests, so he leaves the United Nations, that is the then League of Nations, and turns to narcissistic Germany.

118
00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:44.200
Yes, by the way, the Germans left the League of Nations back in 33.

119
00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:49.190
Hitler recognized the Italian conquest of Ethiopia and thereby the two states grow closer.

120
00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:54.980
Because of that, at the end of 1936 a friendship treaty is signed and the famous Berlin-Rome axis arises.

121
00:10:54.980 --> 00:11:03.910
Something we will not deal with is the Spanish Civil War, where Hitler and Mussolini militarily and financially supported the fascists and their leader Francisco Franco.

122
00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:09.700
So, Italy and Germany were now BFFs, although it is not like there were no snags, but never mind.

123
00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:11.930
Now, Hitler was not a fan of communism.

124
00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:17.710
That same year he signs an anti-communist pact with Japan, directed against the Soviet Union.

125
00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:18.670
How does Japan come in now?

126
00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:21.720
Well, a copy-paste story like for Italy and Germany.

127
00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:25.370
Japan always had a huge population on a very small area.

128
00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:29.180
The economic crisis, logically, had catastrophic consequences here too.

129
00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:37.240
And as this island simply did not have enough resources to support a growing population, the Japanese decided to find those materials in China.

130
00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:37.820
But by force.

131
00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:46.000
And then again the same as we have seen so far: fascism, a staged event as an excuse for war, massive conquest, war crimes, we have no time.

132
00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:58.060
In any case, the most important organization ever, the League of Nations, primarily the United Kingdom and the French, helped China a lot by doing absolutely nothing, and so nobody could stop Japanese expansion.

133
00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:01.170
Italy also joins the anti-communist pact in 1937.

134
00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:07.900
Japan, Italy and Germany now recognize all the newly conquered territories that these three seized and align their plans.

135
00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:12.560
In essence, the biggest fuss was between Hitler and Mussolini over the division of territories.

136
00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.670
First of all, what to do with Austria?

137
00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:20.240
But, as Mussolini said that it is a German land, it was very easy to set further goals.

138
00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:25.420
The Balkans and the Mediterranean go to Italy, and eastern and southeastern Europe, as well as the Danube basin, to Germany.

139
00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:33.160
Oh yes, Italy also occupied Albania in April 1939, thereby taking one of the last steps that led everything to the greatest human tragedy ever.

140
00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:40.950
All these ventures cost Italy dearly, since it simply did not have an economy strong enough to endure all of Mussolini's ambitions.

141
00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:43.990
But wait, how is it even possible that this was allowed?

142
00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:46.980
How is it possible that the British and French did nothing?

143
00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:52.550
You know how it is, people were tired of warring, although in the end both countries began arming.

144
00:12:52.550 --> 00:13:03.350
There were even quite a lot of various agreements and non-aggression pacts between the British and the Germans, and even between Germany and Poland, which, as we know, was a very legitimate deal in the end.

145
00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:08.610
We have mentioned the Soviet Union a little, but it will play a key role in the further course of events.

146
00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:14.260
Namely, for now we have the anti-communist pact of Japan, Italy and Germany, which the Soviet Union fears.

147
00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:19.150
Joseph Stalin had quite a lot of problems in the Far East during the 30s.

148
00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:25.630
Japan expanded so much, even onto far more populous China, which undermined Soviet prestige.

149
00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:29.440
March 1939. Germany targets its next victim, Poland.

150
00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:35.440
Well, after the Treaty of Versailles part of the German population stayed separated from Berlin.

151
00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:39.880
And it was very important to make a corridor that would connect them.

152
00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:49.930
This time Britain actually, to everyone's surprise, sends Warsaw a confirmation that it will help her in case of a German invasion, and France had been in a defensive pact with Poland since the twenties.

153
00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:53.520
Although by now they had seen that they should not wait too long for them.

154
00:13:53.520 --> 00:14:03.140
Plus, since Britain and France, as winners of the great war, remained in a solid relationship and military alliance, these three states now represented some kind of balance in a divided Europe.

155
00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:09.420
That political checkmate angered Hitler so much that he now completely changed his policy toward the Soviet Union.

156
00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:12.180
And suddenly he saw it as a potential partner.

157
00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:20.440
Of course, the irony is that the Soviet Union has a predominantly Slavic population, which, as we know, Hitler hates, but desperate times, desperate measures.

158
00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:28.820
In May 1939 Hitler signs a friendship pact with Italy, known as the Pact of Steel, which was directed against the United Kingdom and France.

159
00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:35.880
Japan did not join him there, because it too still wanted an attack on the Soviet Union, which at that moment clashed with Hitler's interests.

160
00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:39.950
And so we arrive at the second-to-last domino that leads the whole world to ruin.

161
00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:41.720
The famous Molotov-Ribbentrop pact.

162
00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:55.400
On August 23 of the same year, the German foreign minister Ribbentrop and the Soviet foreign minister Molotov sign a non-aggression pact which enabled the division of central Europe between the two states, and the first target was Poland.

163
00:14:55.600 --> 00:15:06.360
Namely, due to the collapse of the Russian Empire and the rise of communism, Russia, that is now the Soviet Union, lost a lot of territory, and then even lost a war to the Poles in the early 1920s.

164
00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:14.050
With the new German-Soviet pact and a joint attack on Poland, Stalin was enabled to regain this territory much more easily.

165
00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:17.600
And so we come to the last domino, the invasion of Poland.

166
00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:26.860
On September 1, 1939, Germany sends over a million and a half soldiers, two thousand planes and two and a half thousand tanks, heading for Warsaw.

167
00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:35.660
Two days later, the United Kingdom and France with all their colonies around the world declare war on Hitler.

168
00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:51.310
On September 17 the Soviet Union finally fulfills its obligation to Germany and strikes eastern Poland, which after heroic efforts nevertheless could not withstand the invasion of two world powers and falls already in October.

169
00:15:51.570 --> 00:16:01.310
This aggression thus drew an enormous part of the world into the conflict and so the Second World War begins, while Yugoslavia and many others join later.

170
00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:09.060
By the end of 1945 this conflict will take between 70 and 85 million lives, of which by some estimates over a million Serbs.

171
00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:14.620
This war will reveal the twisted nature of many people through countless gruesome crimes.

172
00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:22.310
This war will render all agreements meaningless, it will destroy the foundations of many states and it will leave wounds that have still not healed.
